MASTER SPECIFICATION STATEMENT
OneDraft establishes the AI Evaluation, Guardrails & Deterministic Command Verification architecture as the formal control boundary between Aria-generated intelligence and the authoritative OneDraft Project Model.
Aria shall provide the intelligence necessary to interpret customer specifications, reason over project context, generate architectural proposals, interpret redlines and construct structured project commands.
OneDraft shall independently verify those commands against project state, authorization, constraints, geometry, regulatory requirements, coordination requirements and execution policy before permitting them to become authoritative project state.
The resulting architecture is:
CUSTOMER SPECIFICATION → ARIA INTELLIGENCE → STRUCTURED COMMAND → DETERMINISTIC VERIFICATION → PROJECT MODEL → DOCUMENTATION
The Project Model remains the Single Source of Truth.
Aria remains the intelligence layer.
The verification architecture remains the control boundary.
The documentation engine remains the representation layer.
The customer remains the project-originating and review authority within the applicable OneDraft workflow.
